      "title": "Object Types Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Object Types Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Structural Typing",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A value fits if it has the ==required members==; declared name or class is irrelevant",
                "Object type = required members + their types: `{ id: number; name: string }`",
                "`interface` and `type` both name a shape; one variable satisfies either"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Assignability Is Directional",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "interface User { id: number; name: string }",
                "type Named = { name: string }",
                "const u: User = { id: 1, name: \"Ann\" }",
                "const n: Named = u // wider to narrower: OK",
                "const back: User = n // error: id missing"
              ],
              "note": "extra members are fine, missing ones are not"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{green:Wider} (extra members) is assignable to narrower",
                "{red:Narrower} to wider is an error: members missing"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Runtime Reality",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Types are ==erased== at compile time; no runtime check exists",
                "Validate external data separately"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "`as User` on parsed JSON checks nothing; it only silences the compiler."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Interfaces vs Type Aliases",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Interfaces vs Type Aliases",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Same Shape, Two Syntaxes",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`interface User { id: number }` declares an ==object shape==",
                "`type User = { id: number }` does the {green:same}",
                "interface: `interface Admin extends User { role: string }`",
                "alias: `type Admin = User & { role: string }` (==intersection==)"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. What Only One Can Do",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "interface",
                "type"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Extend",
                  "`extends`",
                  "`&`"
                ],
                [
                  "Same name twice",
                  "{green:merges}",
                  "{red:error}"
                ],
                [
                  "Union, primitive, tuple",
                  "{red:no}",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "Mapped, conditional",
                  "{red:no}",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Two `interface User` blocks ==merge== into one",
                "A duplicate `type` alias is an **error**"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "interface User { id: number }",
                "interface User { name: string }",
                "const u: User = { id: 1, name: 'Ann' }",
                "type ID = string | number"
              ],
              "note": "merged User needs both members"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Rule of Thumb",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Which one?",
              "text": "==interface== for public object and class contracts. ==type== for anything else."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Optional and Readonly Properties",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Optional and Readonly Properties",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Optional properties",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`nickname?: string` has type ==string | undefined==",
                "The key may be {green:omitted} entirely",
                "`?` is __not__ the same as nullable"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Type",
                "Key required?",
                "undefined OK?"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`{ a?: string }`",
                  "{green:no}",
                  "yes"
                ],
                [
                  "`{ a: string | undefined }`",
                  "{red:yes}",
                  "yes"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. readonly",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`readonly id: number` blocks ==reassignment==",
                "`readonly` is **shallow**: contents of `tags` stay mutable"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "interface User {",
                "  nickname?: string;",
                "  readonly id: number;",
                "  readonly tags: string[];",
                "}",
                "user.id = 2; // error: read-only",
                "user.tags.push('x'); // allowed"
              ],
              "note": "shallow: only the property is locked"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Lock contents: `ReadonlyArray<string>` or `readonly string[]`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Utility types",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Utility",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`Readonly<T>`",
                  "all properties ==readonly=="
                ],
                [
                  "`Partial<T>`",
                  "all properties ==optional=="
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Compile-time only",
              "text": "`readonly` is erased at runtime. It stops **assignments in your code**, not mutation of the real object."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Unions, Intersections and Literal Types",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Unions, Intersections and Literal Types",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Unions and Intersections",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Value is",
                "Access"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`A | B`",
                  "one of A, B",
                  "common members only"
                ],
                [
                  "`A & B`",
                  "all of A and B",
                  "every member"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Narrow with `typeof`, `in`, `instanceof`, `===` in `if` or `switch`",
                "Conflicting property types in `&` collapse to ==never=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Literal Types",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`type Dir = 'up' | 'down'` allows only those exact values",
                "`const` keeps the literal, `let` widens to `string`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "const x = 'up'; // type 'up'",
                "let y = 'up';   // type string"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Discriminated Unions",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "type Shape =",
                "  | { kind: 'circle'; r: number }",
                "  | { kind: 'square'; s: number };",
                "switch (sh.kind) {",
                "  case 'circle': return sh.r;",
                "  case 'square': return sh.s;",
                "  default: const _x: never = sh;",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "shared literal kind narrows each case"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Exhaustiveness",
              "text": "A `never` default stops compiling when a new kind is added."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Structural Typing and Excess Property Checks",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Structural Typing and Excess Property Checks",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Structural Typing",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Identical structure ⇒ ==interchangeable==",
                "A different **name** does not make types incompatible"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "type A = { id: number }",
                "interface B { id: number }",
                "const a: A = { id: 1 }",
                "const b: B = a  // OK"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Excess Property Checks",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Source",
                "Code",
                "Result"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Fresh literal",
                  "`const u: User = { id: 1, extra: 2 }`",
                  "{red:error}"
                ],
                [
                  "Via variable",
                  "`const u: User = o`",
                  "{green:allowed}"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Checked on ==fresh object literals== only",
                "Bypass: type assertion `as User`",
                "Opt in: index signature `[key: string]: unknown`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Weak Types and Brands",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Weak type== = all properties optional",
                "Value sharing **none** of them is an error",
                "**Brand** types that share a shape but must not mix"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "type UserId = string & { __brand: 'UserId' }",
                "type OrderId = string & { __brand: 'OrderId' }",
                "const u = 'u1' as UserId",
                "const o: OrderId = u  // error"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Fresh literal ⇒ ==excess check==. Same object via a variable ⇒ only **structural fit**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Cheat Sheet: Object Types",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Cheat Sheet: Object Types",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Interface vs Type",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "interface",
                "type"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Extend",
                  "`extends`",
                  "`&`"
                ],
                [
                  "Merge",
                  "{green:yes}, same name",
                  "{red:error}"
                ],
                [
                  "Union, tuple, mapped",
                  "{red:no}",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Properties and Unions",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`prop?: T` means ==T | undefined==, may be omitted",
                "`readonly prop: T` is **shallow** and ==compile-time only==",
                "`A | B` = ==one of==; `A & B` = ==all of==",
                "Discriminate unions with a literal `kind` field, then `switch`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Literals",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "const a = 'up';  // 'up'",
                "let b = 'up';    // string",
                "const o = { k: 'up' } as const;",
                "// { readonly k: 'up' }"
              ],
              "note": "as const freezes to literal readonly types"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Excess Property Check",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Runs on ==fresh literals== only",
                "Via a variable: **structural** compatibility, extras allowed"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "`readonly` is shallow: `tags.push()` still works. Types are erased at runtime."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "With `type User = { id: number }`, does `const o = { id: 1, extra: 2 }; const u: User = o;` compile?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Yes, it compiles",
                "Excess property checks hit only fresh object literals",
                "Writing `{ id: 1, extra: 2 }` directly in the assignment would error"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Does `const x: { a: string | undefined } = {};` compile?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "No, the key `a` is still required",
                "Only `a?: string` lets you omit the key"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "With `readonly tags: string[]`, does `user.tags.push('x')` compile?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Yes, `readonly` is shallow",
                "`user.tags = []` is the error",
                "Use `readonly string[]` to block `push`"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
